// The game <-> dcrpulse gaming bridge contract.
//
// The game is the gRPC CLIENT and dials the bridge over mTLS on a dedicated
// port. Its identity is NEVER a field in any message: it is the client
// certificate, resolved by the bridge from the verified peer. A game therefore
// cannot assert which game it is - it presents a credential and the bridge
// decides. One Subscribe stream carries every bridge->game push; everything the
// game initiates is a unary call. The bridge never dials the game, so a game
// behind NAT needs no inbound port.
//
// The bridge forms an opinion only on the money verbs and on routing. Frame
// contents are opaque: what a frame means is between the players, who sign
// their own traffic and check each other's, and a bridge that inspected
// payloads would be adding a party nobody agreed to trust.
